

00:01:32.475 --> 00:01:37.693
<v MAN> Hi Shannon. How are you settling into your new flat?

00:01:37.693 --> 00:01:39.454
<v WOMAN> Really well, thanks.

00:01:39.454 --> 00:01:41.519
<v MAN> You look like you're going shopping.

00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:48.043
<v WOMAN> Yes, I am. My cousins are coming to stay for a couple of days and I have to cook for them.

00:01:48.043 --> 00:01:54.744
<v MAN> Well, there are plenty of places to buy food in Kite Place. It's the area by the harbour.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:59.692
<v WOMAN> Oh, okay. I'll find that on the map. Thanks.

00:01:59.692 --> 00:02:02.305
<v MAN> What sort of food do you need to get?

00:02:02.305 --> 00:02:06.631
<v WOMAN> Well, neither of them eats meat, but they both like fish.

00:02:06.631 --> 00:02:09.627
<v MAN> Well, there's a really good fish market there.

00:02:09.627 --> 00:02:12.654
<v WOMAN> Oh, great. Where is it exactly?

00:02:12.654 --> 00:02:20.340
<v MAN> It's at the far end of Kite Place. So you have to go over the bridge, and then it's on the right.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.474
<v WOMAN> OK. Is it open all day?

00:02:23.474 --> 00:02:31.326
<v MAN> It doesn't close until four. But I'd recommend going earlier than that. It does run out of some things.

00:02:31.326 --> 00:02:33.351
<v WOMAN> Oh, I don't want that to happen.

00:02:33.351 --> 00:02:40.816
<v MAN> As long as you get there by three-thirty, you should be fine. It's only eleven now, so plenty of time.

00:02:40.816 --> 00:02:41.657
<v WOMAN> Right.

00:02:41.657 --> 00:02:44.359
<v MAN> Do you need to buy vegetables, too?

00:02:44.359 --> 00:02:49.243
<v WOMAN> I do. And I want to avoid all the plastic packaging in the supermarket.

00:02:49.243 --> 00:02:55.192
<v MAN> Well, there's a really nice organic shop there. Now, what's it called?

00:02:55.192 --> 00:02:59.538
<v MAN> It's the name of a flower. I know, it's Rose.

00:02:59.538 --> 00:03:00.971
<v WOMAN> Oh, that's a nice name.

00:03:00.971 --> 00:03:05.234
<v MAN> Yeah, it sells vegetables and quite a lot of other stuff.

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:06.196
<v WOMAN> And where's that?

00:03:06.196 --> 00:03:13.870
<v MAN> Well, as you reach the market, you'll see a big grey building on your left. I think it used to be a warehouse.

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:24.040
<v MAN> Anyway, now it's a restaurant upstairs, but the ground floor has two shops either side of the entrance, and it's the one on the left.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.478
<v WOMAN> Hmm, that's easy enough.

00:03:25.478 --> 00:03:31.904
<v MAN> You can't miss it. There's also a big sign on the pavement, so you can look for that.

00:03:31.904 --> 00:03:37.797
<v WOMAN> Fine. I guess if I need anything else, I'll have to go to the supermarket.

00:03:37.797 --> 00:03:41.762
<v MAN> Yeah, you should be able to get everything you need.

00:03:41.762 --> 00:03:50.209
<v MAN> But there's a minibus that goes to the supermarket if you need it. It's purple, and the number is 289.

00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:53.329
<v WOMAN> Thanks, that's great.

00:04:27.436 --> 00:04:35.336
<v MAN> So, what do you need to get at the fish market? The salmon is always very good. And the shellfish?

00:04:35.336 --> 00:04:40.852
<v WOMAN> I'm going to make a curry, I think. And I need about 12 prawns for that.

00:04:40.852 --> 00:04:42.504
<v MAN> They'll have plenty of those.

00:04:42.771 --> 00:04:43.625
<v WOMAN> Okay.

00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:46.055
<v MAN> Have you ever tried sand fire?

00:04:46.055 --> 00:04:49.055
<v WOMAN> No. What's that?

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:55.747
<v MAN> It's a type of seaweed. I just ask for a handful. And you fry it in butter. It's delicious.

00:04:55.747 --> 00:04:59.784
<v WOMAN> Oh, I might try that. How do you spell it?

00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:09.350
<v MAN> It's S-A-M-P-H-I-R-E.

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:12.981
<v WOMAN> Great. It's always good to try something different.

00:05:12.981 --> 00:05:13.695
<v MAN> Yeah.

00:05:13.695 --> 00:05:20.997
<v WOMAN> I'll see what beans they have in the organic shop. And I think I'll get something for dessert there.

00:05:20.997 --> 00:05:22.932
<v MAN> How about a mango?

00:05:22.932 --> 00:05:30.002
<v WOMAN> I'm not sure. They're not always ripe. I'd prefer a melon. It's bigger too.

00:05:30.002 --> 00:05:39.643
<v MAN> Good idea. The owner also sells a lot of spices there that you can put in a curry. And things like coconut.

00:05:39.643 --> 00:05:42.796
<v WOMAN> Oh that's very helpful. I'll have a look.

00:05:42.796 --> 00:05:43.887
<v MAN> No problem.

00:05:43.887 --> 00:05:50.117
<v WOMAN> I know bread doesn't really go with curry. But I always like to have some in case.

00:05:50.117 --> 00:05:57.561
<v MAN> As I said, all the bread is homemade. And there's lots of variety. I like the brown bread myself.

00:05:57.561 --> 00:05:59.508
<v WOMAN> Mmm, sounds good.

00:05:59.508 --> 00:06:01.682
<v MAN> They sell other things there too.

00:06:01.682 --> 00:06:05.510
<v WOMAN> Like cakes? I love chocolate cake.

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:14.185
<v MAN> Well, not that. But they have a whole range of tarts. And the best are the strawberry ones.

00:06:14.185 --> 00:06:19.605
<v WOMAN> Perfect. Hopefully I won't even have to go to the supermarket.
